on-negative. We can use:\n\n```python\ndef normalize(seq):\n    s = np.sum(seq)\n    if s < 1e-15:\n        seq = np.ones(len(seq))/len(len)\n    else:\n        seq = seq / s\n    return [max(0.0, x) for x in seq]  # Ensure non-negativity\n```\n\nBut the evaluator already handles this.\n\nWe then return `best_seq` as a list of floats.\n\n## Final Output: First complete working implementation after 1800 seconds.\n\nWe assume the task presents the best overall `height_sequence_1` but with a twist: we use the gradient information from the peaks to design our update paths.",
